## 5. Room & Lobby System

### 5.1 Room creation
- Client calls `POST /api/rooms` (REST) to create a room.
- Server generates a **6-character uppercase alphanumeric code** (e.g. `XK92PL`), avoiding ambiguous characters: `0`, `O`, `1`, `I`, `L`.
- Creator's WebSocket is opened immediately after; they are assigned host.
- Room expires after **30 minutes of inactivity** (no connected players) or **2 hours absolute**.

### 5.2 Joining
- Client calls `GET /api/rooms/{code}` to validate the room exists and is in `lobby` phase.
- Then connects to `wss://host/ws?room=XK92PL&name=Alice`.
- Server assigns a UUID, persists the player, broadcasts `PLAYER_JOINED`.

### 5.3 Host transfer
- If the host disconnects, server picks the next connected player in join order.
- Broadcast `PLAYER_LEFT` with `newHostId` set.
- If no players remain, room enters a 5-minute grace period before deletion.

### 5.4 Reconnection
- On reconnect, client sends `JOIN_ROOM` with the same display name.
- Server matches by `(roomCode, displayName)` — if found and game is in progress, player is re-added as the original player. Their private `ROLE_ASSIGNED` is re-sent.
- If the room has moved to a new phase, full `ROOM_STATE` is sent first.

### 5.5 Room limits
| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Min players to start | 4 |
| Max players per room | 10 |
| Max rooms per server | 500 (configurable) |
| Reconnect grace window | 60 seconds |
| Room TTL (empty) | 30 minutes |
| Room TTL (absolute) | 2 hours |

