## 9. Server Architecture

### 9.1 Directory layout

```
susword-server/
├── cmd/
│   └── server/
│       └── main.go
├── internal/
│   ├── hub/
│   │   ├── hub.go           -- registry of all rooms, goroutine-safe
│   │   └── room.go          -- room state and logic
│   ├── player/
│   │   └── player.go        -- player model, read/write pump goroutines
│   ├── game/
│   │   ├── state.go         -- phase types, state machine transitions
│   │   ├── words.go         -- word list + random selection with history
│   │   └── reveal.go        -- reveal order shuffling
│   ├── ws/
│   │   └── handler.go       -- HTTP → WS upgrade, message routing
│   ├── api/
│   │   └── handler.go       -- REST endpoints
│   └── config/
│       └── config.go        -- environment-based configuration
├── go.mod
├── go.sum
└── Makefile
```

### 9.2 Concurrency model

```
HTTP listener
    │
    ▼
ws/handler.go  ──upgrade──▶  Player goroutines (one per connection)
                                 │  readPump  → parses message → sends to Room.inbound chan
                                 │  writePump ← receives from Player.send chan → writes WS frame
                                 ▼
                             Room.run() goroutine (one per room)
                                 │  reads from inbound chan
                                 │  calls state machine transition
                                 │  broadcasts to all Player.send chans
                                 ▼
                             Hub (registry)
                                 │  thread-safe map[roomCode]*Room
                                 │  cleanup goroutine (TTL enforcement)
```

Each room owns exactly one goroutine. All mutations to room state happen in that goroutine — no locks needed on room state itself. The hub uses `sync.RWMutex` only for the room map.

