## 11. Persistence Strategy

**v1: No persistence.** All state lives in-memory. Rooms disappear if the server restarts.

Rationale:
- SusWord sessions are short (10–40 minutes).
- The reconnect window (60 seconds) covers transient network drops without needing a database.
- Adding Redis/Postgres is a natural v2 upgrade path.

**v2 upgrade path** (when needed):
- Store `Room` structs as JSON in Redis with TTL matching `ROOM_TTL_MINUTES`.
- Subscribe to `PLAYER_LEFT` events to refresh TTL.
- Enables horizontal scaling and graceful restarts.

---

## 12. Rate Limiting & Abuse Prevention

| Layer | Limit | Mechanism |
|---|---|---|
| Room creation | 10 rooms per IP per hour | `golang.org/x/time/rate` token bucket |
| WS messages | 20 messages per second per connection | Per-connection token bucket |
| Oversized messages | > 4 KB rejected | Check in readPump before unmarshal |
| Invalid action flooding | 10 consecutive errors → disconnect | Error counter per connection |
| Join attempts | 30 per IP per hour | Token bucket on `/api/rooms/:code` |

