## 14. Frontend Integration Changes

The existing Next.js app needs these changes to support online mode:

### 14.1 New route
Add `/online` page alongside the existing home screen. The existing `/` (offline pass-and-play) is unchanged.

### 14.2 New Zustand store (or context)
Create `lib/onlineStore.ts` mirroring the shape of `lib/store.ts` but driven by WebSocket events instead of local dispatch:

```typescript
// Replaces local reducer with WS-driven state
interface OnlineGameStore extends GameState {
  roomCode: string | null;
  myPlayerId: string | null;
  myRole: "civilian" | "imposter" | null;
  mySecretWord: string | null;
  isHost: boolean;
  connectionStatus: "connecting" | "connected" | "reconnecting" | "disconnected";
  sendAction: (action: ClientMessage) => void;
}
```

### 14.3 WebSocket client
Create `lib/wsClient.ts`:

```typescript
class WSClient {
  connect(roomCode: string, displayName: string): void
  send(msg: ClientMessage): void
  on(type: string, handler: (payload: unknown) => void): void
  off(type: string, handler: Function): void
  disconnect(): void
}
```
- Handles automatic reconnect with exponential backoff (max 5 retries, 30s cap).
- Sends `PING` every 25 seconds to keep the connection alive through proxies.
- Listens for `PONG`; reconnects if no response after 10 seconds.

### 14.4 Timer
In online mode, the `DiscussionTimer` component reads `endsAt` from the store (set by `DISCUSSION_STARTED`) instead of a local `timerStartedAt`. This keeps all clients in sync.

```typescript
// Online timer
const remaining = Math.max(0, Math.floor((endsAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000));
```

### 14.5 UI additions
| Screen | Additions |
|---|---|
| `/online` landing | "Create Room" button → `POST /api/rooms` → redirect to lobby |
| Lobby | Room code display with copy button, player list, host badge, timer picker, Start button |
| Reveal | Each player sees their own reveal without physical phone passing |
| Voting | Host sees the full active player list with "Eliminate" buttons |

